      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If the provider detects a conflict, the upload fails with an [`NSFileWriteUnknownError`](nsfilewriteunknownerror-c.enum.case.md), with the underlying error of [`localVersionConflictingWithServer`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/FileProvider/NSFileProviderError/localVersionConflictingWithServer).",
      "normalizedSource": "If the provider detects a conflict, the upload fails with an [`NSFileWriteUnknownError`](nsfilewriteunknownerror-c.enum.case.md), with the underlying error of [`localVersionConflictingWithServer`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/FileProvider/NSFileProviderError/localVersionConflictingWithServer).",
      "sourceHash": "6a842e51f1044c00b7132462b4fbf7264cac15d10d02019d8339db994ffae4f2",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "If the upload succeeds, the sync resumes with the [`NSFileManagerResumeSyncBehavior.preserveLocalChanges`](nsfilemanagerresumesyncbehavior/preservelocalchanges.md) behavior.",
      "contextAfter": "In this case, the app needs to call [`fetchLatestRemoteVersionOfItem(at:completionHandler:)`](filemanager/fetchlatestremoteversionofitem(at:completionhandler:).md), rebase local changes on top of the newly fetched version to resolve the conflict, and try again to resume sync.",
      "documentTitle": "NSFileManagerResumeSyncBehavior.afterUploadWithFailOnConflict",
      "framework": "Foundation",
